/-! # Polygraph/Omega/IdempotentSemigroupDemonstrator — the walking idempotent semigroup as a
one-critical-pair Squier demonstrator (OMEGA-4 continued, WP-SQUIER r2 — the family round)

★ **The third walker re-encoded as an `OmegaComputad` Squier demonstrator — the walking idempotent
semigroup `<e | e.e => e>` at ONE critical pair, the first HALF-GLOBULAR walker.**  After the involution
`<s | s.s => id>` and the walking monad `<t | eta, mu>`, this file ships the idempotent semigroup: one
object, one endo-1-generator `e`, one 2-generator `M : e.e => e` (the idempotent law oriented
left-to-right), and its SOLE Squier critical pair `eee` exhibited as a generating 3-cell — mirroring the
involution demonstrator constructor-for-constructor, at one row.

## Why HALF-GLOBULAR (the new scope observation this walker introduces)

The involution and the walking monad's modulo-strict pairs reduce to `id` on one side of the peak, so
their VALLEYS close only modulo the strict UNIT laws (`(id)s ~ s ~ s(id)`).  The idempotent's rule RHS is
a GENERATOR `e`, not `id` — so both whisker orders of `M` on `e` land on the LITERALLY IDENTICAL 1-cell
`vcomp e e` (`boundaryTarget M = e`, and both `whiskerRight M e` and `whiskerLeft e M` rebuild
`vcomp e e` at their target boundary).  The valley closes ON THE NOSE (`refl`); only the PEAK
`(e.e).e ~ e.(e.e)` is modulo the strict ASSOCIATIVITY law.  This is the first walker whose critical pair
is half-globular: one boundary literal, one boundary modulo-strict (witnessed by
`idempotentSemigroupOmegaEeeValley_literallyEqual = true` and
`idempotentSemigroupOmegaEeeLegs_notLiterallyParallel = false`).

## The presentation as a 2-polygraph (Squier reading)

  * 0-cells: one object `idempotentSemigroupOmegaPoint`.
  * 1-cells: freely generated by `idempotentSemigroupOmegaEGen : point => point`; words are `e^n`.
  * 2-cells (the rewrite rule): ONE generator `idempotentSemigroupOmegaMuGen : e.e => e` (the idempotent
    law).  No `id` anywhere — the RHS is the generator `e` (contrast the involution, whose RHS `id` forces
    the `idOne` 1-cell).
  * 3-cells: the critical-pair filler (this file), ONE of them.

## The sole critical pair, enumerated by hand (recon JOB 2)

The rule's source pattern is `ee` (length 2).  Overlaps of `ee` with itself:

  * **Length-1 overlap `eee` — the SOLE genuine critical pair.**  Reduce the front `ee`
    (`idempotentSemigroupOmegaEeeLeftLeg = M |> e : (ee)e => (e)e`) or the back `ee`
    (`idempotentSemigroupOmegaEeeRightLeg = e <| M : e(ee) => e(e)`).  Both land on `vcomp e e` (literal!).
    JOINABLE at `vcomp e e`, the valley `refl`.
  * Length-2 overlap (`ee = ee`): the SAME redex — not a genuine critical pair.
  * Length-0 overlap (`eeee`): a DISJOINT-redex diamond, resolved by orthogonality — not a critical pair.

So there is exactly ONE critical pair, `eee`, and ONE generating 3-cell filling it
(`idempotentSemigroupOmegaEeeThreeCell`).  The correspondence to the Homology lane's
`IdempotentSemigroupChainComplex` (`idempotentSemigroupCriticalPairCountIsOne`, `eee: (ee)e→ee, e(ee)→ee
@ ee`, `H1 = 0` by the unit factor) is NAMED here, not imported (the r1 read-only discipline).

## The honest coherence scope (mirroring the involution, refined to half-globular)

The single critical pair is parallel only MODULO the strict congruence at the PEAK (`(ee)e` and `e(ee)`
are structurally distinct, `idempotentSemigroupOmegaEeeLegs_notLiterallyParallel` computes `false`), but
LITERALLY parallel at the VALLEY (both `vcomp e e`).  The POSITIVE content shipped here:

  * the generating 3-cell `idempotentSemigroupOmegaEeeThreeCell` firing the critical-pair row through
    `ofRelation`;
  * the peak join `(ee)e ~ e(ee)` (`idempotentSemigroupOmegaEeePeakJoin`, a single associativity row) and
    the valley join `vcomp e e ~ vcomp e e` (`idempotentSemigroupOmegaEeeValleyJoin`, `refl` — the
    half-globular collapse);
  * the assembled per-pair resolution and the least-congruence universal property
    (`idempotentSemigroupOmegaCriticalPairsIdentifiedInEveryModel`).

## The 2-path normalizer wall — the full homotopy basis (design note, no code this round)

The FULL homotopy basis (every parallel 2-path pair `e^n => e^k` 3-cell-homotopic) is WALLED identically
to the involution and the monad and stays the OMEGA-5 handoff.  The exact obligations the full basis
needs (the named design deliverable, shared with `CyclicThreeDemonstrator`; ONE pair here so obligation 3
below is trivially met by the single `eee` 3-cell):

  1. **`TwoPath` NF-directed syntax** — a subset of `SaturatedConvOverWithId` derivations oriented as
     reduction sequences with a canonical (leftmost-outermost) 2-path per parallel class.
  2. **A structural fuel measure** `twoPathSize : TwoPath → Nat` (constant-`Nat` motive, like `cellSize`)
     strictly decreasing under Squier peak-elimination — so the recursion is STRUCTURAL FUEL, not
     `WellFounded.fix` (whose `propext` / `Quot.sound` leak is the Init-only wall).
  3. **Completeness of the generating 3-cells** — every 2-path critical branching is the shipped `eee`
     3-cell (here a one-line check; the `CyclicThreeDemonstrator` shows why the COUNT becomes load-bearing
     once there is more than one critical word).
  4. **The orthogonality 3-cells** (UNSHIPPED) — the disjoint-redex commutation squares (`eeee` width-0
     diamond) needed for the closure — the concrete missing datum.
  5. **Newman-at-dim-3** (local confluence + termination ⇒ confluence through the normal form) — feasible
     ONLY if obligation 2 gives a structural-fuel decoder rather than `WellFounded.fix` (the Wall A/B of
     `SquierAscentLedger` / `InvolutionSquierBasis`).

Blocking node: a `conv_toParityNF`-analogue at the 2-path level (a normalizer on reduction sequences one
dimension up) plus general Squier coherence needing OMEGA-2 Steiner arithmetic at n=2 AND termination of
3-cell rewriting, where Forest-Mimram (arXiv:2109.05369) stayed pen-and-paper (cite Guiraud-Malbos).

Raw Lean 4 + Init.  Per-declaration `#assert_no_axioms` gated in the audit twin. -/

namespace FX1Poly.Polygraph.Omega

/-! ## The walking-idempotent-semigroup 2-polygraph as an `OmegaComputad` -/

/-- The **walking-idempotent-semigroup omega-computad**: one object (`Unit`), one generator label at every
dimension (`Unit`).  A single 2-generator `M`, so a constant `Unit` label family suffices (like the
involution's, and unlike the monad's `Bool` — the monad split `eta` / `mu`) — no `Nat`-match in
`genLabel`, so propext-clean. -/
def idempotentSemigroupOmegaComputad : OmegaComputad where
  modeCarrier := Unit
  genLabel := fun _ => Unit

/-- The trivial mode comparator (one object). -/
def idempotentSemigroupOmegaModeBeq :
    idempotentSemigroupOmegaComputad.modeCarrier → idempotentSemigroupOmegaComputad.modeCarrier → Bool :=
  fun _ _ => true

/-- The trivial heterogeneous generator comparator — the leg-distinctness probes are STRUCTURAL (whisker
orders differ), so the comparator need not separate labels. -/
def idempotentSemigroupOmegaGenBeq :
    (dimA dimB : Nat) → idempotentSemigroupOmegaComputad.genLabel dimA →
      idempotentSemigroupOmegaComputad.genLabel dimB → Bool :=
  fun _ _ _ _ => true

/-- The single object `*`. -/
def idempotentSemigroupOmegaPoint : CellExpr idempotentSemigroupOmegaComputad 0 := CellExpr.ofMode ()

/-- The endo-1-generator `e : * => *`. -/
def idempotentSemigroupOmegaEGen : CellExpr idempotentSemigroupOmegaComputad 1 :=
  CellExpr.gen (dim := 0) () idempotentSemigroupOmegaPoint idempotentSemigroupOmegaPoint

/-- The 1-cell `e.e` (the rule's left-hand side). -/
def idempotentSemigroupOmegaEeWord : CellExpr idempotentSemigroupOmegaComputad 1 :=
  CellExpr.vcomp idempotentSemigroupOmegaEGen idempotentSemigroupOmegaEGen

/-- ★ The **rewrite rule** `M : e.e => e` as the single 2-cell generator.  Globular: `e.e` and `e` are
both `* => *`.  The RHS is the GENERATOR `e` — no `id` anywhere (contrast the involution, whose RHS is
`id`), the source of this walker's half-globular valley. -/
def idempotentSemigroupOmegaMuGen : CellExpr idempotentSemigroupOmegaComputad 2 :=
  CellExpr.gen (dim := 1) () idempotentSemigroupOmegaEeWord idempotentSemigroupOmegaEGen

/-! ## The two legs of the sole critical pair `eee` -/

/-- The **left leg**: reduce the FRONT `ee` of `eee` — `M` whiskered on the right by `e`
(`(ee)e => (e)e`, target `vcomp e e`). -/
def idempotentSemigroupOmegaEeeLeftLeg : CellExpr idempotentSemigroupOmegaComputad 2 :=
  CellExpr.whiskerRight idempotentSemigroupOmegaMuGen idempotentSemigroupOmegaEGen

/-- The **right leg**: reduce the BACK `ee` of `eee` — `M` whiskered on the left by `e`
(`e(ee) => e(e)`, target `vcomp e e`). -/
def idempotentSemigroupOmegaEeeRightLeg : CellExpr idempotentSemigroupOmegaComputad 2 :=
  CellExpr.whiskerLeft idempotentSemigroupOmegaEGen idempotentSemigroupOmegaMuGen

/-- The left leg's source 1-cell is the front-associated peak `(ee)e`. -/
theorem idempotentSemigroupOmegaEeeLeftLeg_boundarySource :
    boundarySource idempotentSemigroupOmegaEeeLeftLeg
      = CellExpr.vcomp idempotentSemigroupOmegaEeWord idempotentSemigroupOmegaEGen := rfl

/-- The right leg's source 1-cell is the back-associated peak `e(ee)`. -/
theorem idempotentSemigroupOmegaEeeRightLeg_boundarySource :
    boundarySource idempotentSemigroupOmegaEeeRightLeg
      = CellExpr.vcomp idempotentSemigroupOmegaEGen idempotentSemigroupOmegaEeWord := rfl

/-- ★ The left leg's target 1-cell is `vcomp e e` — and so is the right leg's (the half-globular valley
collapse). -/
theorem idempotentSemigroupOmegaEeeLeftLeg_boundaryTarget :
    boundaryTarget idempotentSemigroupOmegaEeeLeftLeg
      = CellExpr.vcomp idempotentSemigroupOmegaEGen idempotentSemigroupOmegaEGen := rfl

/-- ★ The right leg's target 1-cell is `vcomp e e` — LITERALLY the same term as the left leg's target. -/
theorem idempotentSemigroupOmegaEeeRightLeg_boundaryTarget :
    boundaryTarget idempotentSemigroupOmegaEeeRightLeg
      = CellExpr.vcomp idempotentSemigroupOmegaEGen idempotentSemigroupOmegaEGen := rfl

/-! ## The critical-pair row and the generating 3-cell -/

/-- ★ The **`eee` critical-pair row** — a `CellRelOver` firing on the two reduction legs.  The walking
idempotent semigroup's homotopy basis: ONE generating 3-cell. -/
inductive IdempotentSemigroupCriticalRow :
    {d : Nat} → CellExpr idempotentSemigroupOmegaComputad d →
      CellExpr idempotentSemigroupOmegaComputad d → Prop where
  /-- The `eee` critical pair: the front-redex leg and the back-redex leg. -/
  | eee : IdempotentSemigroupCriticalRow idempotentSemigroupOmegaEeeLeftLeg
      idempotentSemigroupOmegaEeeRightLeg

/-- The base relation the 3-cell resolves: the strict omega laws united with the single critical-pair
row. -/
def idempotentSemigroupOmegaBaseRel : CellRelOver idempotentSemigroupOmegaComputad :=
  unionCellRel idempotentSemigroupOmegaComputad
    (StrictAxiomRel idempotentSemigroupOmegaComputad) IdempotentSemigroupCriticalRow

/-- ★ **THE GENERATING 3-CELL.**  The `eee` critical pair fired through `ofRelation`: a genuine
`SaturatedConvOverWithId` convertibility between the two legs.  Non-vacuous — the two legs are
structurally distinct 2-cells. -/
def idempotentSemigroupOmegaEeeThreeCell :
    SaturatedConvOverWithId idempotentSemigroupOmegaComputad idempotentSemigroupOmegaBaseRel
      idempotentSemigroupOmegaEeeLeftLeg idempotentSemigroupOmegaEeeRightLeg :=
  SaturatedConvOverWithId.ofRelation (Or.inr IdempotentSemigroupCriticalRow.eee)

/-! ## The joinability witnesses (the critical pair is resolved — peak modulo strict, valley on the nose) -/

/-- ★ **THE PEAK JOIN** — the two leg SOURCES join by a single associativity row: `(ee)e ~ e(ee)`.  The
two peak spellings are convertible in the strict congruence (though structurally distinct). -/
def idempotentSemigroupOmegaEeePeakJoin :
    SaturatedConvOverWithId idempotentSemigroupOmegaComputad idempotentSemigroupOmegaBaseRel
      (boundarySource idempotentSemigroupOmegaEeeLeftLeg)
      (boundarySource idempotentSemigroupOmegaEeeRightLeg) :=
  SaturatedConvOverWithId.ofRelation
    (Or.inl (StrictAxiomRel.vcompAssoc idempotentSemigroupOmegaEGen idempotentSemigroupOmegaEGen
      idempotentSemigroupOmegaEGen))

/-- ★ **THE VALLEY JOIN (on the nose)** — the two leg TARGETS are the LITERALLY IDENTICAL 1-cell
`vcomp e e`, so the valley closes by `refl`.  This is the half-globular collapse: the rule's RHS is a
generator, so no strict-unit detour is needed on the valley (contrast the involution's `(id)s ~ s ~
s(id)`). -/
def idempotentSemigroupOmegaEeeValleyJoin :
    SaturatedConvOverWithId idempotentSemigroupOmegaComputad idempotentSemigroupOmegaBaseRel
      (boundaryTarget idempotentSemigroupOmegaEeeLeftLeg)
      (boundaryTarget idempotentSemigroupOmegaEeeRightLeg) :=
  SaturatedConvOverWithId.refl _

/-! ## The assembled per-pair resolution and the least-congruence universal property -/

/-- ★ A **coherent resolution** of one idempotent-semigroup critical pair, joinable modulo the strict
congruence at the peak and on the nose at the valley: the two leg SOURCES are convertible, the two legs
are convertible (the generating 3-cell), and the two leg TARGETS are convertible.  Parameterised by the
two legs (the involution's `InvolutionCoherentResolution` generalised, the monad's
`MonadCriticalPairResolved` at one pair). -/
structure IdempotentSemigroupCriticalPairResolved {d : Nat}
    (leftLeg rightLeg : CellExpr idempotentSemigroupOmegaComputad (d + 1)) : Prop where
  /-- The two leg SOURCES are convertible. -/
  peakJoined : SaturatedConvOverWithId idempotentSemigroupOmegaComputad idempotentSemigroupOmegaBaseRel
    (boundarySource leftLeg) (boundarySource rightLeg)
  /-- The two legs are convertible (the generating 3-cell). -/
  legsConvertible : SaturatedConvOverWithId idempotentSemigroupOmegaComputad
    idempotentSemigroupOmegaBaseRel leftLeg rightLeg
  /-- The two leg TARGETS are convertible. -/
  valleyJoined : SaturatedConvOverWithId idempotentSemigroupOmegaComputad idempotentSemigroupOmegaBaseRel
    (boundaryTarget leftLeg) (boundaryTarget rightLeg)

/-- The `eee` pair is coherently resolved (peak associativity, valley refl — half-globular). -/
theorem idempotentSemigroupOmegaEeeResolved :
    IdempotentSemigroupCriticalPairResolved idempotentSemigroupOmegaEeeLeftLeg
      idempotentSemigroupOmegaEeeRightLeg :=
  ⟨idempotentSemigroupOmegaEeePeakJoin, idempotentSemigroupOmegaEeeThreeCell,
    idempotentSemigroupOmegaEeeValleyJoin⟩

/-- ★ **THE SINGLE 3-CELL GENERATES THE IDENTIFICATION (least-congruence UP).**  For any relation
`targetRel` absorbing the idempotent base relation (a congruence containing the strict laws and the `eee`
row), the two legs of the idempotent critical row are `targetRel`-related — so the generating 3-cell is
the datum whose fold through `SaturatedConvOverWithId.recInto` identifies the critical pair in EVERY
model.  Uniform in the row (keyed on `IdempotentSemigroupCriticalRow`). -/
theorem idempotentSemigroupOmegaCriticalPairsIdentifiedInEveryModel
    {targetRel : CellRelOver idempotentSemigroupOmegaComputad}
    (absorbs : IsSaturatedCongruenceWithId idempotentSemigroupOmegaComputad
      idempotentSemigroupOmegaBaseRel targetRel)
    {d : Nat} {leftLeg rightLeg : CellExpr idempotentSemigroupOmegaComputad d}
    (row : IdempotentSemigroupCriticalRow leftLeg rightLeg) : targetRel leftLeg rightLeg :=
  SaturatedConvOverWithId.recInto absorbs (SaturatedConvOverWithId.ofRelation (Or.inr row))

/-! ## The native one-count and the cofork column (correspondence NAMED to the Homology lane) -/

/-- The single critical-pair label, re-declared NATIVELY over this substrate (mirroring the Homology
lane's `IdempotentSemigroupCriticalPairs`; the correspondence is named, not imported). -/
inductive IdempotentSemigroupOmegaCriticalPairLabel
  /-- The `eee` overlap — the sole critical pair. -/
  | eee

/-- The complete enumeration of the idempotent-semigroup critical pairs over this substrate — ONE,
listed. -/
def allIdempotentSemigroupOmegaCriticalPairs : List IdempotentSemigroupOmegaCriticalPairLabel := [.eee]

/-- ★ **The critical-pair count is exactly ONE** — kernel-checked (`rfl`), re-derived natively (it
matches the Homology lane's `idempotentSemigroupCriticalPairCountIsOne`). -/
theorem idempotentSemigroupOmegaCriticalPairCountIsOne :
    allIdempotentSemigroupOmegaCriticalPairs.length = 1 := rfl

/-- ★ **The enumeration is EXHAUSTIVE** — the single label appears. -/
theorem allIdempotentSemigroupOmegaCriticalPairsExhaustive :
    ∀ pair : IdempotentSemigroupOmegaCriticalPairLabel, pair ∈ allIdempotentSemigroupOmegaCriticalPairs
  | .eee => List.Mem.head _

/-- The abelianized cofork column of the single critical pair — a single `Nat` (one 2-generator `M`, so
the column is the net `#M` count; both whisker legs fire `M` once, so the net cancels to `0`).  The
correspondence to the Homology lane's `idempotentSemigroupCriticalPairBoundaryColumn` (`Int`-valued Smith
column, `H1 = 0` by the unit factor) is NAMED here, not proven across substrates. -/
def idempotentSemigroupOmegaCriticalPairCoforkColumn : IdempotentSemigroupOmegaCriticalPairLabel → Nat
  | .eee => 0

/-! ## The coherent-presentation statement (the honest-scope bundle) -/

